      "observed": "The EPD boost switch Q2 has value 'MCH3478-TL-W', but its library part is 'MCH3478-TL-H', its footprint is 'MCH3478-TL-W:On_Semiconductor-MCH3478-TL-H-Manufacturer_Recommended', and its metadata says 'Package Type SC-70FL / MCPH-3' with a 0.65 mm pitch package, not SOT-23.",
      "expected": "The specification requires Q1/Q2 to be the MCH3478-TL-W N-channel MOSFET in a SOT-23 package for the EPD boost-converter switch.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(value \"MCH3478-TL-W\") ... (libsource (lib \"MCH3478-TL-W\") (part \"MCH3478-TL-H\") ... (field (name \"Package Type\") \"SC-70FL / MCPH-3\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Q1 | MCH3478-TL-W (N-channel MOSFET, SOT-23, 30 V/2 A) | EPD boost-converter switch"}
      ],
      "impact": "The board may be fabricated/assembled with the wrong MOSFET package or variant, causing a sourcing/assembly mismatch for the EPD boost switch.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U10"],
      "pins": ["U10.13", "U10.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "SKW92A pins 13 and 14, named LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX- in the library part, are both connected directly to the GND net.",
      "expected": "Unused Ethernet PHY differential pairs should not be tied to ground; the specification describes unused PHY nets as single-node/unconnected nets in this export and the RJ45 jack is not wired.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the LAN1_RX+/-, LAN1_TX+/- global labels used elsewhere resolve to single-node nets containing only U5 (SKW92A) pins"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the module drives or enables those Ethernet PHY outputs, the differential pair is shorted to ground, which could load the PHY, alter module behavior, or cause a functional deviation from the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.52
    },
    {
      "category": "footprint_mismatch",
      "components": ["C6"],
      "pins": ["C6.1", "C6.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C6-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C6 is a 0.1 uF capacitor with library part Device:C, but its footprint is 'Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder', and pin 1 is unconnected.",
      "expected": "A capacitor should use a capacitor footprint and, if intended as a bypass/decoupling part, should be connected between a supply and ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(ref \"C6\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "C6 unconnected-_C6-Pad1_ 0 0.1u"}
      ],
      "impact": "This is a component-identity/footprint error; if C6 was intended as a decoupling capacitor, its unconnected pin and mismatched footprint could reduce high-frequency bypassing or cause assembly confusion.",
      "confidence": 0.38
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show at least one clear deviation: the EPD boost MOSFET Q2 uses a non-SOT-23 SC-70FL/MCPH-3 footprint and TL-H library part despite the spec requiring MCH3478-TL-W in SOT-23. Additional suspicious issues include an Ethernet PHY differential pair shorted to ground and a capacitor with an inductor footprint and one unconnected pin."
}

